WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.024
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.324 --> 00:00:09.768
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.068 --> 00:00:17.248
Unit six: Comparatives and Superlatives. Today you will compare two or more people, places and things.

4
00:00:17.548 --> 00:00:20.143
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.263
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:25.990
Compare.

7
00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:29.865
Compare means to show how things are alike or different.

8
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.055
Compare the two cities.

9
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.407
Your turn. Say: Compare.

10
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:39.140
Compare.

11
00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:40.687
Taller.

12
00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:43.149
Taller means more tall.

13
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.343
Dara is taller than Rith.

14
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.579
Your turn. Say: Taller.

15
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:52.225
Taller.

16
00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:54.066
The tallest.

17
00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.549
The tallest means more tall than all others.

18
00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.929
He is the tallest in class.

19
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:03.808
Your turn. Say: The tallest.

20
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:07.749
The tallest.

21
00:01:08.483 --> 00:01:09.705
More expensive.

22
00:01:10.717 --> 00:01:13.413
More expensive means costing more than another.

23
00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:15.819
This bag is more expensive.

24
00:01:16.417 --> 00:01:19.173
Your turn. Say: More expensive.

25
00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.301
More expensive.

26
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.365
The most beautiful.

27
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.278
The most beautiful means more beautiful than all others.

28
00:01:29.883 --> 00:01:31.790
Angkor Wat is the most beautiful.

29
00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:35.419
Your turn. Say: The most beautiful.

30
00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:40.150
The most beautiful.

31
00:01:40.917 --> 00:01:41.860
As ... as.

32
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.815
As ... as means equal in some way.

33
00:01:45.417 --> 00:01:47.172
He is as tall as his father.

34
00:01:47.783 --> 00:01:50.180
Your turn. Say: As ... as.

35
00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.197
As ... as.

36
00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:55.603
Than.

37
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:58.790
Than means used to compare two things.

38
00:01:59.383 --> 00:02:00.628
She is older than me.

39
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:03.033
Your turn. Say: Than.

40
00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:06.531
Than.

41
00:02:07.283 --> 00:02:08.447
Irregular.

42
00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:12.100
Irregular means not following the usual rule.

43
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:13.905
Good becomes better.

44
00:02:14.517 --> 00:02:17.134
Your turn. Say: Irregular.

45
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.291
Irregular.

46
00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.449
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.283 --> 00:02:28.794
Visal, how do we make comparatives?

48
00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:40.642
For short adjectives we add -er, such as taller and faster. For long adjectives we use more, such as more expensive. We use than to compare two things.

49
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.204
And superlatives?

50
00:02:44.317 --> 00:02:56.489
We use the plus -est for short adjectives, such as the tallest, and the most for long ones, such as the most beautiful. We use a superlative to compare three or more things.

51
00:02:57.583 --> 00:02:59.304
Are there irregular forms?

52
00:03:00.417 --> 00:03:10.444
Yes. Good becomes better and the best, and bad becomes worse and the worst. We also say as tall as to show that two things are equal.

53
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.263
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.117 --> 00:03:20.284
Grammar focus: Comparative: -er and more plus than; superlative: the -est and the most.

55
00:03:20.584 --> 00:03:21.910
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.617 --> 00:03:24.477
Dara is taller than his brother.

57
00:03:25.383 --> 00:03:28.370
Angkor Wat is the most beautiful temple in Cambodia.

58
00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:36.165
Use -er and than to compare two things, and the -est or the most for three or more. Learn the irregular forms good, better, best.

59
00:03:36.917 --> 00:03:40.242
Be careful! Don't say: He is more tall than me.

60
00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.118
Say: He is taller than me.

61
00:03:44.418 --> 00:03:46.023
Short adjectives take -er.

62
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:49.462
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.779
Comparing Friends.

64
00:03:52.079 --> 00:03:53.765
Dara is taller than his brother.

65
00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.463
He is also the tallest player in the football team.

66
00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.826
His new bag is more expensive than mine.

67
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:05.551
Rithy is as fast as Dara, but Sokha is the fastest.

68
00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:09.391
Everyone agrees that the match was the best of the season.

69
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.374
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:15.217 --> 00:04:17.030
Dara is blank than his brother.

71
00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.763
A, taller. B, tallest. C, more tall.

72
00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.021
The answer is A: taller.

73
00:04:27.183 --> 00:04:29.264
This is blank film I have ever seen.

74
00:04:29.564 --> 00:04:32.985
A, best. B, the best. C, the better.

75
00:04:36.533 --> 00:04:38.475
The answer is B: the best.

76
00:04:39.617 --> 00:04:41.221
Beautiful becomes blank.

77
00:04:41.521 --> 00:04:45.860
A, beautifuler. B, most beautiful only. C, more beautiful.

78
00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.085
The answer is C: more beautiful.

79
00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.646
Who is the fastest?

80
00:04:54.946 --> 00:04:58.193
A, Sokha. B, Dara. C, Rithy.

81
00:05:01.733 --> 00:05:03.501
The answer is A: Sokha.

82
00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.104
Good becomes blank.

83
00:05:06.404 --> 00:05:09.895
A, more good. B, better. C, gooder.

84
00:05:13.433 --> 00:05:15.119
The answer is B: better.

85
00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:19.671
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.517 --> 00:05:22.272
Compare two places you know.

87
00:05:31.083 --> 00:05:32.595
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:32.895 --> 00:05:44.072
Phnom Penh is bigger than my hometown, and it is also more crowded. But my hometown is quieter and cleaner. I think it is the best place to live because it is peaceful.

89
00:05:44.372 --> 00:05:46.035
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:54.548
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and comparative: -er and more plus than; superlative: the -est and the most.

91
00:05:54.848 --> 00:06:00.891
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

92
00:06:01.191 --> 00:06:03.611
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:03.911 --> 00:06:06.134
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

